---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Waitlist from '../components/Waitlist.astro'
import { BMC_LINK } from '../config'
---

<Base
  title="VIP waitlist"
  description="My VIP classroom is not open yet. Here is what goes in it, and how to hear the day it opens."
  path="/vip"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="badge">Not open yet</span>
      <h1>The VIP classroom</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        It is in draft. You cannot buy it today, and I would rather say that
        plainly than take your money for a room that is half built.
      </p>

      <h2>What goes in it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>My live setup.</strong> The real Hermes configuration I use
          every day, not a clean demo version made for a video.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>My actual folder structures.</strong> The ICM builds behind my
          own work, including the ugly parts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Finished builds.</strong> Take them, run them, change them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Request rights.</strong> You ask for a build. I make it. It
          lands in the classroom for everyone in there.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What is not in it yet</h2>
      <p>
        Structured course material. I am writing it now. If you want a finished
        library on day 1, you should wait for me rather than join early and feel
        short changed.
      </p>

      <h2>The price</h2>
      <p>
        The plan is 29 dollars a month, and that is a founding price. It goes up
        as the material fills in, and anyone who joins at 29 keeps 29 for as
        long as they stay.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--muted)">
        None of that is live yet, so there is nothing to click. The list below
        is the only thing that does anything today.
      </p>

      <Waitlist id="vip-page-waitlist" />

      <hr />

      <h2>In the meantime</h2>
      <p>
        The free material is genuinely free and it is enough to get you running.
        Start with <a href="/start">the 3 folder build</a>. If you want to see
        where I teach, that is
        <a href={BMC_LINK} rel="sponsored noopener">BuildMarketClose</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="disclosure">
        That BuildMarketClose link is an affiliate link. I earn a commission if
        you join through it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
